\details{
With \code{k = "auto"}, plskit's \code{pls1_find_k_optimal()} (selector \code{"r2_se"},
five-fold cross-validation) picks the number of components, and the
p-value is plskit's confirmatory test at k = 1, independent of that
choice. With a whole number \code{k}, the model has \code{k} components and the test
runs at \code{k}. The test is plskit's \code{test_method = "auto"} (Lenartowicz and
Plisiecki, 2026), which runs \code{split_exact} or \code{split_nb}, chosen from the
vectors alone; \code{test$name} says which ran.
